<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The graph of <m>y = {\sin}\,x</m> is mapped onto <m>y = {3\sin 5x}</m> by two stretches.</p><div>(a) The stretch with the <m>x</m>-axis invariant has stretch factor <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div><div>(b) The stretch with the <m>y</m>-axis invariant has stretch factor <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/>  </div><div>(c) The point <m>{(90^\circ, 1)}</m> on <m>y = {\sin}\,x</m> is mapped to ( <fillin characters="6" name="ans3"/> <m>^\circ</m> , <fillin characters="6" name="ans4"/> )   </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Every point moves away from the invariant axis by the same factor.</p><p>(a) Multiplying by <m>{3}</m> outside the function multiplies every <m>y</m>-coordinate by <m>{3}</m>: a stretch with the <m>x</m>-axis invariant, stretch factor <m>{3}</m>.</p><p>(b) Replacing <m>x</m> by <m>{5}x</m> makes the wave repeat <m>{5}</m> times as often, so every <m>x</m>-coordinate is multiplied by <m>{\frac{1}{5}}</m>: a stretch with the <m>y</m>-axis invariant, stretch factor <m>{\frac{1}{5}}</m>.</p><p>(c) <m>{(90^\circ, 1)} \mapsto \left({90}^\circ \times {\frac{1}{5}},\ {1} \times {3}\right) = \left({18}^\circ, {3}\right)</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{5}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>18</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>